[08:41:33] Playbook updated from 12 viral Shorts:
[08:41:33]   - State the central topic or resolve the hook's premise within the first 5 seconds to prevent immediate early drop-off.
[08:41:33]   - Make abstract numbers or scales feelable by comparing them to everyday objects like ballpoint pens, cars, or food.
[08:41:33]   - Use a contradiction, hidden mystery, or counter-intuitive fact as the opening line to drive strong initial curiosity.
[08:41:33]   - Structure scripts with clear cause-and-effect progression: introduce a problem, show the failure, and reveal the physical or mechanical solution.
[08:41:33]   - Keep our narration pace between 2.4 and 2.8 words per second to ensure clear delivery without feeling rushed.
[08:41:33]   - Avoid open-ended, overly philosophical questions near the end which kill engagement; use concrete payoffs instead.
[08:41:33]   - Always conclude the video by immediately transitioning into our mandatory brand sign-off without dragging out the ending.
